Package: cinemar
Type: Package
Title: Create CINeMA .cnm Files from Frequentist and Bayesian NMA
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Thodoris", "Papakonstantinou", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "antrcl@tpapak.com")
Description: Builds CINeMA v3 exchange files (.cnm) from network meta-analysis
    results. The frequentist structural block (hat matrix, study contributions,
    design-by-treatment test, heterogeneity) is always computed with 'netmeta',
    which CINeMA needs for the within-study bias, indirectness and incoherence
    domains. When a Bayesian fit is supplied (e.g. a 'gemtc' result as produced
    by MetaInsight) the posterior effects, credible/predictive intervals,
    nodesplit, SUCRA, DIC and tau are written to the Bayesian block and used as
    the primary results. The output validates against cinema_schema_v3.json and
    can be uploaded directly into CINeMA.
License: AGPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    netmeta (>= 3.3),
    meta,
    jsonlite
